# I. Early entrepreneurship (2010-2019): From grid shop to tidal game

> Source: Oral History of Entrepreneurial Enterprise - Why Wang Ning? Why Bubble Matt? (October 2020), Wall Street interview on IPO night

# Start up #

"My goal was pure -- to make my life a little more storytelling. I hope to say to my grandson when I was 80: "Your grandfather is a storyteller."

# First store

In 2010, Wang Ning, 23 years old, opened the first Bubble Matt in the Middle Beijing village of the O.M. Shopping Center, initially a grocery store - a shop for stationery, accessories, toys, everything.

"We were going to be "A," we were going to do "B," and suddenly we did it again in C. That's the norm of starting a business."

# Focus on the turn of the tide

In 2015, Wang Ning made key decisions — cutting off all non-tidal categories and focusing on the whole.

"We found that Sonny Angel had a particularly high repurchase rate, and I asked myself, "If we open a shop, we'll sell all of this stuff?"

In 2016, Wang Ning found Hong Kong designer Kenny Wong on Twitter and took Molly’s exclusive IP authorization. This became the starting point for Bubble Matttten.

# The financing is cold

"We went to a bar at five points after signing the investment agreement, and in a noise, I suddenly raised a sound: 'Mike, you invested me today, and if I were Jay, you'd be the Go Jong-jung."

"The last time an investment agency communicated, it asked a very bad question: Why did you choose a big company like Bubble Matt instead of Aufi? I decided to reject their investment."

"There's too many pigeons. But looking back now, it's like the best thing to do."

"Selecting investors is like being a blind date -- seeing the right eyes, you know me, I know you. But love at first sight is not always right, time is important, and I'm in love with you because we have to go through a lot of stories together."

