# Three, Springs Infinite Dialogue (2023): "No Use" and two major barriers

Source: The Springs Fund 'Infinite Dialogue' forum, closed-door sharing.

# The "no use" thing is eternal

"If Molly's head was removed from a flash drive, would you buy so much?"

"All consumer behavior is about solving two things: satisfaction, existence. We are far more sensitive than we thought."

"Arts are eternal. Products with functional properties mean short and inherently decaying life cycles. Only things that are "no use" can go through longer. That's the charm of art, and that's the charm of our industry."

"A cup that increases productivity, it drops from $100 to $10. But a Labubu on the same cup can sell it again to $100."

"Only psycho-consumptions have a bigger market."

# Two big barriers to competition

** Soft threshold — artist resources:**

"We dig up and commercialize great designers like the "record company." Artists are scarce resources that money can't buy."

"We chose artists in the early stages of the tide show by the number of people, and these accumulated artists' resources are difficult to replicate."

** Hard threshold - business accumulation:**

"Ten words: respect time, respect business."

"Retailing ends up in the details of inventory, account periods, supply chains. What the decade has done, don't think about doing it for two or three years."

"We've been in business since the first day of Bubble Matt's business... and all this information is transparent, we're playing cards. But 13 years later, we haven't met a competitor of any size. Why?"

# Market-wide logic

From the Tide Circle to the Fashion Circle to the Happy Circle.

"Happy might be a bigger market."

This has resulted in multiple lines of business such as parks, games, authorizations, etc.

# The branding "language" system

"We created trade languages that include 'snuff boxes, shake boxes, end boxes, end boxes, hidden money, hot money, thunder money'. These languages help spread and sink corporate culture."

"The Bubble Matt's Language" starts with the blind box. Of course, the success of the business is about the product and design."

# Business model nature

"The blind box is not our business model. Our success is not our success, but the success of the balance of business and art."

"Bubby Matt is essentially a design company."

"Now defined as - an industry company with an IP at its core."

# # IP management

"We divide IP into S, A, B, C, and we allocate resources according to hierarchy. The life cycle of an IP depends on the company's input into it and whether it is healthy and sustainable."

