# V, Xinhua Net interview (2025.7): "Become a bubble Matt of the world"

> Source: Xinhuanet, 23 July 2025

# From "China Disney" to "The World's Bubbles Matt"

"In 2020, I said that if China had the most Disneylike business in China, it would be Bubble Matt. Since last year, we wanted to be not Disney in China, but Bubble Matt in the world."

"On the one hand, because of the success of internationalization; on the other hand, I think the way the platform hatches the IP is more adapted to the times."

"If you just follow someone else's path, you can't do it."

# The offshore business is breaking out

"Expert sales will probably outpace the domestic sales rate in 2025. Growth is much faster than expected. IPOs sold less than $2 billion in total, and in 2024 they collected $13 billion. They have now built a lot of bubbles of Matt."

"North America's sales rate this year will be higher than in South-East Asia."

# To the sea, to the advantage of both

"We have two important advantages: Chinese markets and Chinese manufacturing. Artists in other countries, either in markets that are not big enough or in manufacturing that are not mature. China’s excellent manufacturing and powerful markets can be platforms for artists around the world to hatch IPs."

"From the world to the world -- from the world, then to the world."

# The theory of the sea

"Slow is fast, little is much, but focus on one thing and do it slowly."

"We have very few shops, all of them in direct business. There are an estimated 200 shops abroad by the end of this year, building their own teams and running their own businesses. Foreign colleagues last year, more than 1,000, may at least double this year."

"People's quest for happiness and beauty is beyond their borders."

# About Labbu

"Labubu sold over $3 billion last year."

"Labubu may sell nearly 10 million a month after September, and the world is in need. We're trying to get it out of the way so it doesn't get badly fired."

"The cultural industry cannot be rationally calculated, and it cannot spend money to create a Labbu."

"IP businesses usually live long lives, and excavations for the Labubu story and value are just beginning."

# And the way the industry sees it

"A small class of goods, it is possible to create a big business. Respect time, respect for business. Invest enough time in small things, and have the best chance."

"I believe in the power of design and beauty. The driving force behind the next big development of many industries is beauty. It was nothing, now it's beauty."

# Business growth metaphor

"Some companies are like grass, growing fast, but not worth much; some are like flowers, though beautiful, but short. We want to be tree-like enterprises, and we want to root them deep enough."

"We believe in the dynamics and accumulated forces. We are pioneers in the tidal trades, and many things have no way to learn, but to touch the river with stones."

# To the young man

"Every era has the opportunity of every era. Believe in the value of effort, in curiosity, in the good. Every generation may not be the same in its pursuit of life -- the generation that has more value for efficiency and cost, and our generation more for innovation and beauty. Together, all of us seek and create good!"

